      "578": "Written repeated bars allow forward tracking. Simple repeat signs use continuous counts starting with initial statement, first bar of each system written again. Braced repeat signs require both staves repeating.",
      "579": "Repeated sections/rests/ending structures must correspond between score and parts for rehearsal orientation; do not collapse distinct repeated sections.",
      "580": "Tacet has whole-movement/remainder conditions. Attacca entry requires duration/landmarks; mid-movement long rests keep count. Accidentals after extracting voices need context review.",
